\section{How we built the dataset}
% ============================================================================

\subsection{Collecting}

Sources arrive in different shapes, so the system picks one of five strategies
per source: download a bulk file, call a documented endpoint, run a
purpose-written parser ($36$ of these are implemented), hand the page to a
tool-using language-model agent, or suspend the source. The agent is capped at
$10$ reasoning steps, $12$ plain page fetches, and $8$ browser-rendered fetches
per site; when it succeeds it writes down the extraction rule it found, so the
next run takes the cheap path.

Strategies change based on what actually happens, and the transitions are
driven by observed outcomes rather than set by hand
(Figure~\ref{fig:collection}).

